      "target": "../sections/sec-001-2-the-generalized-skyrme-system.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "In this section, we give some details of the one-parameter interpolating family of Skyrme systems. The field is denoted $\\Phi_{\\beta}=(\\Phi_1,\\Phi_2,\\Phi_3,\\Phi_4)$, where each component $\\Phi_{\\beta}$ is a function of the spatial coordinates $x^j=(x^1,x^2,x^3)=(x,y,z)$, and the constraint $\\Phi_{\\beta}\\Phi_{\\beta}=1$ is imposed. The energy density for the system, parametrized by $\\alpha\\in[0,1]$, is\n\n$$\\label{Enden}\n  {\\cal E}=\\lambda_2[(\\partial_j\\Phi_{\\beta})(\\partial_j\\Phi_{\\beta})-\\alpha P_jP_j]\n  +\\lambda_4[2(1-\\alpha)F^j_{\\beta\\gamma}F^j_{\\beta\\gamma}+\\alpha Q^jQ^j],$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\\begin{",
